{"task_id": "HumanEval/14", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef all_prefixes(string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list of all prefixes from shortest to longest of the input string.\n\n    Args:\n        string: The input string.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of strings, where each element is a prefix of the input string,\n        ordered from the shortest to the longest.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> all_prefixes('abc')\n        ['a', 'ab', 'abc']\n        >>> all_prefixes('')\n        []\n        >>> all_prefixes('x')\n        ['x']\n        >>> all_prefixes('hello')\n        ['h', 'he', 'hel', 'hell', 'hello']\n    \"\"\"\n    result_prefixes: List[str] = []\n    for i in range(len(string)):\n        # String slicing string[:i+1] creates a new substring (prefix)\n        # from the beginning of the string up to and including the character at index i.\n        result_prefixes.append(string[:i+1])\n    return result_prefixes\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/14", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef all_prefixes(string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all prefixes of an input string, ordered from shortest to longest.\n\n    Args:\n        string: The input string.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of strings, where each element is a prefix of the input string,\n        ordered from shortest to longest. Returns an empty list if the input\n        string is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    prefixes = []\n    # Iterate from 1 up to and including the length of the string\n    # This ensures that for a string of length N, we get N prefixes\n    # of lengths 1, 2, ..., N.\n    for i in range(1, len(string) + 1):\n        # Extract the substring from the beginning of the string up to index i (exclusive)\n        # This gives a prefix of length i.\n        prefixes.append(string[0:i])\n    return prefixes\n```"}
