{"task_id": "HumanEval/15", "solution": "```python\ndef string_sequence(n: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a space-delimited string of numbers from 0 up to a given integer n, inclusive.\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): A non-negative integer representing the upper bound of the sequence.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: A string containing the space-delimited sequence of numbers.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is an integer but is negative.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> string_sequence(0)\n        '0'\n        >>> string_sequence(5)\n        '0 1 2 3 4 5'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Generate a sequence of numbers from 0 to n (inclusive),\n    # convert each to a string, and join them with a single space.\n    return ' '.join(str(i) for i in range(n + 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/15", "solution": "```python\ndef string_sequence(n: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a space-delimited string of numbers from 0 up to n (inclusive).\n\n    Args:\n        n: An integer representing the upper bound of the sequence (inclusive).\n\n    Returns:\n        A string containing the space-delimited sequence of numbers.\n        Examples:\n        - If n = 0, returns '0'\n        - If n = 5, returns '0 1 2 3 4 5'\n        - If n < 0, returns '' (empty string)\n    \"\"\"\n    # Generate a sequence of integers from 0 to n (inclusive).\n    # If n is negative, range(n + 1) will be an empty range,\n    # which correctly leads to an empty string when joined.\n    numbers = range(n + 1)\n\n    # Convert each number in the sequence to its string representation.\n    string_numbers = map(str, numbers)\n\n    # Join the string representations with a single space character.\n    result_string = ' '.join(string_numbers)\n\n    return result_string\n```"}
