{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "```python\ndef count_distinct_characters(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of distinct characters in a string, considering alphabetic\n    characters case-insensitively. Non-alphabetic characters are treated distinctly\n    based on their literal value.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string: The string from which distinct characters are to be counted.\n\n    Returns:\n        A non-negative integer representing the count of distinct characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    distinct_chars = set()\n    for char in input_string:\n        # Convert character to lowercase if it's alphabetic.\n        # Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged by .lower()\n        # (e.g., '1'.lower() is '1', '#'.lower() is '#').\n        processed_char = char.lower()\n        distinct_chars.add(processed_char)\n    return len(distinct_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "```python\ndef count_distinct_characters(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of distinct characters in a given string, ignoring case.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to analyze.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The total count of distinct characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_chars = set()\n    for char in input_string:\n        seen_chars.add(char.lower())\n    return len(seen_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "```python\ndef count_distinct_characters(string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of distinct characters in a given string, ignoring case.\n\n    This function iterates through the input string, converts each character\n    to lowercase to ensure case-insensitivity, and adds it to a set.\n    The size of the set at the end represents the total count of unique,\n    case-insensitive characters.\n\n    Args:\n        string: The input string to analyze.\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing the total count of distinct characters.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"Hello, World!\")\n        10\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"xyzXYZ\")\n        3\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"Jerry\")\n        4\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"\")\n        0\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"aaaaa\")\n        1\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"AaBbCc\")\n        3\n        >>> count_distinct_characters(\"123123\")\n        3\n    \"\"\"\n    distinct_chars = set()\n    for char in string:\n        distinct_chars.add(char.lower())\n    return len(distinct_chars)\n\n```"}
