{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nWORD_TO_INT_MAP = {\n    'zero': 0, 'one': 1, 'two': 2, 'three': 3, 'four': 4,\n    'five': 5, 'six': 6, 'seven': 7, 'eight': 8, 'nine': 9\n}\n\nINT_TO_WORD_MAP = [\n    'zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four',\n    'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine'\n]\n\ndef sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a space-delimited string of number words (e.g., 'zero', 'one') \n    from smallest to largest numerical value.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers (str): A space-delimited string of number words \n                       (e.g., 'three one five').\n                       Input is assumed to contain only valid number words \n                       from 'zero' to 'nine' and be correctly space-delimited.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: A new string with these number words sorted from smallest to \n             largest numerical value, separated by single spaces \n             (e.g., 'one three five').\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return \"\"\n\n    # FR1: Input Processing - Split input string into individual words\n    number_words: List[str] = numbers.split(' ')\n\n    # FR2: Word-to-Integer Conversion\n    integer_values: List[int] = []\n    for word in number_words:\n        # Assumed valid input based on NFR4 - no explicit error handling for invalid words\n        integer_values.append(WORD_TO_INT_MAP[word])\n\n    # FR3: Sorting Logic - Sort the numerical values in ascending order\n    integer_values.sort()\n\n    # FR4: Integer-to-Word Conversion\n    sorted_words: List[str] = []\n    for int_val in integer_values:\n        sorted_words.append(INT_TO_WORD_MAP[int_val])\n\n    # FR5: Output Formatting - Concatenate sorted words into a single string\n    result_string: str = ' '.join(sorted_words)\n\n    # FR6: Return Value\n    return result_string\n```"}
