{"task_id": "HumanEval/27", "solution": "```python\ndef flip_case(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flips the case of alphabetic characters in a given string.\n\n    Converts all lowercase alphabetic characters to uppercase and all\n    uppercase alphabetic characters to lowercase. Non-alphabetic\n    characters remain unchanged.\n\n    Args:\n        string (str): The input string to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: A new string with the case of alphabetic characters flipped.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> flip_case('Hello')\n        'hELLO'\n        >>> flip_case('Python 3.9')\n        'pYTHON 3.9'\n        >>> flip_case('')\n        ''\n        >>> flip_case('\u00c4\u00f6\u00fc')\n        '\u00e4\u00d6\u00dc'\n    \"\"\"\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in string:\n        if char.isupper():\n            result_chars.append(char.lower())\n        elif char.islower():\n            result_chars.append(char.upper())\n        else:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/27", "solution": "```python\ndef flip_case(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flips the case of English alphabet characters in a string.\n    Lowercase characters become uppercase, and uppercase characters become lowercase.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new string with the cases of alphabetic characters flipped.\n    \"\"\"\n    flipped_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':  # Check for lowercase English alphabet\n            flipped_chars.append(char.upper())\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':  # Check for uppercase English alphabet\n            flipped_chars.append(char.lower())\n        else:  # Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged\n            flipped_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(flipped_chars)\n```"}
