{"task_id": "HumanEval/29", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef filter_by_prefix(strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters an input list of strings, returning only those that start with a given prefix.\n\n    Args:\n        strings: A list of strings to be filtered.\n        prefix: The prefix string to match against.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing only the strings from the input list that start with the prefix,\n        maintaining their original relative order.\n\n    >>> filter_by_prefix([], 'a')\n    []\n    >>> filter_by_prefix(['abc', 'bcd', 'cde', 'array'], 'a')\n    ['abc', 'array']\n    >>> filter_by_prefix(['apple', 'banana', 'apricot'], 'ap')\n    ['apple', 'apricot']\n    >>> filter_by_prefix(['test', 'toast'], 't')\n    ['test', 'toast']\n    >>> filter_by_prefix(['hello', 'world'], '')\n    ['hello', 'world']\n    >>> filter_by_prefix(['foo', 'bar'], 'xyz')\n    []\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_strings: List[str] = []\n\n    for s in strings:\n        if s.startswith(prefix):\n            filtered_strings.append(s)\n\n    return filtered_strings\n```"}
